{"repositoryId":240644944,"availability":"available","full":"mmichlin66/mimcss","name":"mimcss","description":"Authoring CSS with TypeScript","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":11,"forks":1,"created":"2020-02-15T04:32:29Z","updated":"2026-10-03T19:57:39Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://www.mimcss.com/demo/mimcss/playground.html","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T07:15:20.041Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T07:15:20.041Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T07:15:20.041Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-16T07:15:20.041Z","stars":11,"forks":1}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Mimcss is a CSS-in-JS library that allows authoring CSS styles without creating CSS files. You code your style rules including CSS tags, classes, animations, media etc. by creating TypeScript classes. The Mimcss library processes these classes and creates the rules that are inserted into elements in the of your HTML document. As a result, all advantages of dynamic JavaScript coding combined with type-safety and convenience of TypeScript coding apply to CSS authoring. In addition, your application or library bundle is self contained and doesn't require a separate CSS bundle."],"features":["Compatible with and independent of any library: use with React, Angular, Vue etc.","Co-exists with regular CSS files - doesn't require re-writing of all existing styles at once or at all. You can gradually introduce Mimcss into you project.","Stylesheets are defined as TypeScript classes.","Stylesheets are dynamically activated (inserted into DOM) and can be deactivated (removed from DOM) if desired.","Styled components are supported where each component instance gets its individual set of CSS rules isolated from other instances."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mmichlin66/mimcss/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"635d183371d926eef17d0b4f4135e77f849bd47055e0d52aa0030a29f9372bb8","extractedAt":"2026-10-16T07:15:20.139Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T07:15:20.139Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Mimcss is a CSS-in-JS library that allows authoring CSS styles without creating CSS files. You code your style rules including CSS tags, classes, animations, media etc. by creating TypeScript classes. The Mimcss library processes these classes and creates the rules that are inserted into elements in the of your HTML document. As a result, all advantages of dynamic JavaScript coding combined with type-safety and convenience of TypeScript coding apply to CSS authoring. In addition, your application or library bundle is self contained and doesn't require a separate CSS bundle.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mmichlin66/mimcss/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"635d183371d926eef17d0b4f4135e77f849bd47055e0d52aa0030a29f9372bb8","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mmichlin66/mimcss/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-16T07:15:20.140Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-03T19:57:39Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mmichlin66/mimcss/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-16T07:15:20.142Z","hash":"635d183371d926eef17d0b4f4135e77f849bd47055e0d52aa0030a29f9372bb8","originalBytes":19609,"storedBytes":19609,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["css","mimcss","this.","class","style","color","properties","rules","mystyles","styles","names","classes","custom","extends","typescript","css.styledefinition","property","red","tsx","guide","see","using","values","tag","type","code","define","library","other","rule","following","import","pseudo","several","types","used","blue","defined","application","build","colors","dom","features","fontweight","number","numbers","these","var","which","while","change","defaultcolor","equivalent","etc.","examples","floating","hover","named","names.","only","point","provides","regular","set","support","supported","supports","there","units","va